Yet beneath your feet—you feel it. A single step appears. Not stone. Not wood.

A thread of golden light, thin as a spider’s silk, stretching into infinite mist.

The Hermit’s lantern glows gently in your palm—its light does not illuminate the path ahead.

It reveals what was always there.

To your left: the ghostly image of every choice you ever abandoned—the cups you walked away from, the voices you silenced, the dreams you buried under duty, fear, or exhaustion.

To your right: the wildfire of every reckless leap you took—burning too fast, too bright, leaving scorched earth behind, chasing the thrill, never the truth.

And between them—the thread.

You breathe.

The Knight of Wands flares—*move!*

The Hermit holds firm—*wait.*

The Eight of Cups weeps silently—*let go.*

You close your eyes.

Not to block the visions.

To hear yourself.

